meta {
  name: Inspect Container
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/docker/containers/{{container_id}}/inspect
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{jwt_token}}
}

docs {
  Operational inspect view for a single container. The response is a strict
  whitelist over bollard's full inspect output — see ContainerInspectInfo in
  src/routes/dtos/docker.rs.

  Returned:
    id, name, image, created, restart_count
    state    { status, running, paused, restarting, started_at,
               finished_at, exit_code, health }
    ports    [ { container_port, protocol, host_port } ]
    networks [ { name, network_id } ]

  NOT returned (intentionally — sensitive):
    environment variables, mounts, host config (privileged, devices,
    cap_add, security_opts), network IPs / driver_opts, secrets, labels.

  If the mobile UI needs additional fields, extend the DTO and the
  map_inspect helper in src/routes/rest/docker.rs.
}
